case:bunge-states-of-a-thing
    a atlas:Example ;
    rdfs:label "a set of states of a thing"@en ;
    atlas:gloss "a set of states of a thing" ;
    atlas:sourceLocation "ch. 1, §1.2, Example following Definition 1.1, p. 7" ;
    atlas:evidenceCode atlas:HVP ;
    atlas:encodedBy "Shingai Thornton (Claude-assisted)" ;
    atlas:encodedOn "2026-08-01"^^xsd:date .

case:bunge-events-ordered
    a atlas:Example ;
    rdfs:label "a collection of events, even if ordered"@en ;
    atlas:gloss "a collection of events, even if ordered" ;
    atlas:instantiates obj:ordered-non-bonding ;
    atlas:sourceLocation "ch. 1, §1.2, Example following Definition 1.1, p. 7" ;
    atlas:evidenceCode atlas:HVP ;
    atlas:encodedBy "Shingai Thornton (Claude-assisted)" ;
    atlas:encodedOn "2026-08-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment """Half of the catalogue's first separating instance: Klir admits an ordered
collection, Bunge refuses one. The refusal is ontic — an aggregate is a collection "not held
together by bonds" (p. 4), Definition 1.1 requires the members connected, and Definition
1.2(iii) carries 𝔅≠∅; ordering is not bonding — so he refuses ordered BOOKS for the same
reason. See mappings/ordered-collection.md.

The location was deliberately withheld until human-checked: these cases come from the labelled
Example block that follows Definition 1.1 in §1.2, not from Definition 1.1 itself, so entry
003's location did not cover them. Checked against the source and entered 2026-08-05."""@en .
